README for The Periodic Table of Motif Widgets


			       PERIODIC v2.0
			       -------------

	This directory contains the sources for periodic.  Periodic is a
	demo of the displayable widgets in Motif.  Periodic presents many
	Motif widgets for your visual and sensual enjoyment.

    Current startup modes
    ---------------------
    periodic                         Toolkit modern-light defaults
    periodic --appearance modern-dark
    periodic --density compact
    periodic --appearance classic    Toolkit classic defaults
    periodic --historical-resources  Historical fonts and dimensions

    Modern mode uses application class XmdPeriodicModern and has no fallback
    font, color, border or control-size styling. It selects the toolkit profile
    and density before Mrm constructs the UIL hierarchy. The UIL still owns the
    table's content and arrangement. Ordinary Xt options (-display, -geometry,
    -xrm) remain available; explicit application resources take precedence.

    Historical mode uses class XmdPeriodic, classic appearance and the original
    fallback resources. To customize it, install XmdPeriodic.ad as XmdPeriodic
    in an app-defaults directory. Do not merge historical resources globally
    when comparing toolkit defaults. --historical-resources cannot be combined
    with a non-classic --appearance.

    Run beside periodic.uid, or use UIDPATH to make it discoverable. Startup
    reports missing UID data and failed hierarchy construction as errors.

	This is a rewrite of the previous version that was shipped with
	earlier releases of Motif.  The original version of Periodic can
	be found in ../../tests/Performance/Expose/.

	Enjoy,

	Michael K. Yee
	Alastair Gourlay

